be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:98:- Added GitHub Workflow with `ubuntu-latest`/GCC 7.4.0 as CI step.
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:237:- Fixed an integer overflow. #1447
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:301:- Added support for **reading from `FILE*`** to support situations in which streams are nit available or would require too much RAM. #1370 #1392
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:305:- The `eofbit` was not set for input streams when the end of a stream was reached while parsing. #1340 #1343
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:314:- Added a warning for implicit conversions to the documentation: It is not recommended to use implicit conversions when reading **from** a JSON value. Details about this recommendation can be found [here](https://www.github.com/nlohmann/json/issues/958).  #1363
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:565:- Added check to detect memory **overflow when parsing UBJSON containers** (#962). The optimized UBJSON format allowed for specifying an array with billions of `null` elements with a few bytes and the library did not check whether this size exceeded `max_size()`.
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:651:- :bug: The **"copy" operation of JSON Patch** ([RFC 6902](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6902)) requests that it is an error if the target path points into a non-existing array or object (see #894 for a detailed description). This release fixes the implementation to detect such invalid target paths and throw an exception.
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:686:This section describes changes that change the public API of the library and may require changes in code using a previous version of the library. In section "Moving from 2.x.x to 3.0.0" at the end of the release notes, we describe in detail how existing code needs to be changed.
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:708:- We improved the **diagnostic information for syntax errors** (#301). Now, an exception [`json::parse_error`](http://nlohmann.github.io/json/doxygen/classnlohmann_1_1basic__json_af1efc2468e6022be6e35fc2944cabe4d.html#af1efc2468e6022be6e35fc2944cabe4d) is thrown which contains a detailed message on the error, but also a member `byte` to indicate the byte offset in the input where the error occurred.
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:712:- The binary exchange formats **CBOR and MessagePack can now be parsed from input streams and written to output streams** (#477).
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:713:- Input streams are now only read until the end of a JSON value instead of the end of the input (#367).
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:729:- The build workflow now relies on CMake and CTest. Special flags can be chosen with CMake, including coverage (`JSON_Coverage`), compilation without exceptions (`JSON_NoExceptions`), LLVM sanitizers (`JSON_Sanitizer`), or execution with Valgrind (`JSON_Valgrind`).
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:798:- If an overflow occurs during parsing a number from a JSON text, an exception [`json::out_of_range`](http://nlohmann.github.io/json/doxygen/classnlohmann_1_1basic__json_a28f7c2f087274a0012eb7a2333ee1580.html#a28f7c2f087274a0012eb7a2333ee1580) is thrown so that the overflow is detected early and roundtripping is guaranteed.
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:849:- :bug: Parsing incorrect JSON numbers with leading 0 (`0123`) could yield a [buffer overflow](https://github.com/nlohmann/json/issues/452). This is fixed now by detecting such errors directly by the lexer.
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:889:- :bug: A bug in the CBOR parser was fixed which led to a buffer overflow.
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:911:- :bug: Fixed a lot of **bugs in the CBOR and MesssagePack parsers**. These bugs occurred if invalid input was parsed and then could lead in buffer overflows. These bugs were found with Google's [OSS-Fuzz](https://github.com/google/oss-fuzz), see #405, #407, #408, #409, #411, and #412 for more information.
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:937:- :bug: fixed an [integer overflow error](https://github.com/nlohmann/json/issues/389) detected by [Google's OSS-Fuzz](https://github.com/google/oss-fuzz)
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:939:- :bug: fixed an overflow detection error in the number parser
be/src/lib/json/docs/mkdocs/docs/home/releases.md:1099:  - The precision of output streams is now preserved by the parser.
